{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.VertexIsExceptionalDivisor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.VertexIsExceptionalDivisor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.vertex_completeness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.vertex_completeness","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L91-L104","doc":"**Vertex completeness.**\n\nEvery interaction changing quantum numbers at `p` is realised by a\nfinite braid word whose Hecke image acts within ℛ_p: for every\ntarget endomorphism `target : V → V`, there is a finite list of\nvertex actions whose composite equals `target` and which is\nconfined to the divisor support.\n\nNamed as a `Prop` (pattern C); a proof awaits the braid-word\ngeneration infrastructure.  Ref: [leitner2026] Ch 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.skein_confined_to_reeb_bundle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.skein_confined_to_reeb_bundle","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L75-L89","doc":"**Skein resolution confined to the Reeb bundle.**\n\nEvery Skein resolution `L₊ - L₋ = (q - q⁻¹) L₀` is evaluated within\nthe Reeb bundle ℛ_p over 𝒮_p: the three resolved actions\n(`plus`, `minus`, `smoothed`) all preserve the divisor support, and\nthey satisfy the Hecke/Skein linear relation in `R_q`.\n\nNamed as a `Prop` (pattern C); the carrier records the three\nresolutions and a `Skein` linear-relation witness map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.vertex_is_exceptional_divisor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.vertex_is_exceptional_divisor","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L59-L73","doc":"**Vertex operator factors through the exceptional divisor.**\n\nThe Hecke action on `V^{⊗n}` factors through 𝒮_p: for every\n`T_i ∈ H_n(q)`, the action on `V^{⊗n}` is supported on\n`π⁻¹(p) = 𝒮_p` (it maps divisor states to divisor states) and\nprojects trivially to `A₀` (the base-algebra component is fixed).\n\nNamed here as a `Prop` over the abstract support datum (pattern C);\na proof awaits the Hecke–Reeb-bundle infrastructure (Ch 6 §2).\nRef: [kassel1995] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0783-2 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:vertex-is-exceptional-divisor","label":"prop:vertex-is-exceptional-divisor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAction.act","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAction.act","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The endomorphism induced by the Hecke generator `T_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexAction","kind":"structure","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L53-L57","doc":"A Hecke generator's action on the state space, abstracted as an\nendomorphism `act : V → V` of the divisor-support datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DivisorSupport.toBase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DivisorSupport.toBase","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Projection of the state space onto the base algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DivisorSupport.onDivisor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DivisorSupport.onDivisor","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The exceptional-divisor sub-space membership predicate on `V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DivisorSupport.A₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DivisorSupport.A₀","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The base algebra `A₀` (the \"off-divisor\" component). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DivisorSupport.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DivisorSupport.V","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Total state space `V^{⊗n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DivisorSupport.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DivisorSupport.mk","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DivisorSupport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DivisorSupport","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L39-L51","doc":"Abstract support datum for the brane point `p`: the total state\nspace `V` of `V^{⊗n}`, the sub-space `S_p` cut out by the\nexceptional divisor 𝒮_p, the base algebra `A₀`, and the projection\n`toBase : V → A₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-is-exceptional-divisor.lean#L23-L25","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}